{
 "spec": "Project: Apogee RHBD I/O \u2014 real flow\n# Apogee RHBD I/O \u2014 Real Flow\n\n**Project Name:** Apogee RHBD I/O \u2014 real flow\n\n**Goal**\n- Design two radiation\u2011hardened 5\u202fV analog I/O blocks (LS_UP level\u2011shifter and POR power\u2011on\u2011reset) in the SkyWater sky130 (g5v0d10v5) process.\n- Integrate them into a top\u2011level I/O cell set (TOP_IO).\n- Provide full characterization, regression automation, and sign\u2011off documentation.\n\n**Scope**\n- **LS_UP Level Shifter** \u2013 1.8\u202fV core to 5\u202fV output, functional across a supply sweep of 1.4\u20115.5\u202fV and all PVT corners (ss/tt/ff, \u201355\u202f\u00b0C/27\u202f\u00b0C/125\u202f\u00b0C) and tolerant to SEU injection.\n- **POR Power\u2011On\u2011Reset** \u2013 Reset held until VDD exceeds a calibrated threshold; implemented with native and regular Vt detectors, qualified over the same PVT range.\n- **TOP_IO Integration** \u2013 Combines LS_UP and POR, with complete DRC/LVS sign\u2011off.\n- **Supporting Code** \u2013 Python/NGSPICE scripts for characterization, PVT/SEU table generation, plotting, pytest validation; Verilog glue for reset logic and testbenches; Verilog\u2011A behavioral models; Makefile\u2011driven regression and sign\u2011off automation.\n\n**Process Flow**\n1. **Simulation Stories** \u2013 Netlist creation, supply sweep, PVT & SEU simulations, generation of characterization data.\n2. **Layout Stories** \u2013 Follow\u2011on from simulation (finish\u2011to\u2011start); produce DRC\u2011clean, LVS\u2011matched layouts using Magic and Netgen.\n3. **Code Stories** \u2013 Depend on completed block results; develop scripts, RTL glue, and regression framework.\n\nAll work is performed by AI\u2011driven \u201cemployees\u201d. Design assets live under `analog/`; code resides in `scripts/`, `rtl/`, and `models/`. No PCB or KiCad evaluation board is in scope.\nInstructions: <p>All work is done by AI Employees. Design data lives in the project repository under analog/; code under scripts/, rtl/, models/.</p><ul><li><p>Simulation stories come before layout stories of the same block (finish-to-start).</p></li><li><p>Coding stories depend on the block stories whose results they use.</p></li><li><p>Keep scope to LS_UP, POR and the top-level; no PCB / KiCad evaluation board.</p></li></ul><p></p>\n\nEpic: LS_UP Level\u2011Shifter Design, Simulation, Layout & Modeling\nDevelop the radiation\u2011hardened 1.8\u202fV\u2011to\u20115\u202fV level\u2011shifter (LS_UP) for the SkyWater sky130 (g5v0d10v5) process. The work spans schematic capture, parameterised SPICE netlist creation, exhaustive supply/PVT/SEU simulations, DRC\u2011clean Magic layout, LVS sign\u2011off, a Verilog\u2011A behavioral model, and a Python characterization script. All artifacts are stored under `analog/`, `scripts/`, and `models/`. The epic must satisfy the project goal of delivering a fully\u2011characterised analog block with zero DRC/LVS violations and reusable models for downstream users.\nExpectations: A complete LS_UP block ready for top\u2011level integration, with verified simulation data, layout files, behavioral model and automation script delivered on schedule.\n\nStory: Create LS_UP schematic and parameterized SPICE netlist\nThe Lead Analog Designer will capture the complete 1.8\u202fV\u2011to\u20115\u202fV LS_UP level\u2011shifter schematic, incorporate radiation\u2011hardening techniques, and generate a parameterized SPICE netlist that spans the 1.4\u20115.5\u202fV supply range. The netlist must include placeholders for PVT corners and SEU injection points, be stored under `analog/`, and pass a quick sanity NGSPICE run. This work establishes the design foundation for all downstream simulation, layout, and modeling activities.",
